The script spawns `[<sys.prefix>/bin/ohyesmlx, "app"]` with no `env=`, no `-I`, no `-B` — a console script over a wheel built from `git archive HEAD`, under `/opt/homebrew/bin/python3.14`. The launcher, the spec (05-06-PLAN AC-6: "via the bundled interpreter, exactly the launcher's argv and env"), and the bundle all say otherwise.

New test file `tests/test_fable_s6_f5.py` (5 tests, pass on current code) drives `main()` with `Popen` stubbed and asserts the real argv, the absent `env=`, the absence of any bundle-pointing flag, and the launcher's contrasting argv read from the Swift source. Red-checked: mutating the spawn to `-I -B -m ohyesmlx.cli app` failed three tests at `smoke_clean_account.py:843`, then restored byte-exact (`git diff --stat scripts/` empty).

Two things I found beyond the finding's own list, both evidenced in the report: the bundled Python verifies TLS against `/etc/ssl/cert.pem` while the smoke's Homebrew Python uses `/opt/homebrew/etc/openssl@4/cert.pem` (two different CA bundles), and `_finish` records no artifact identity, so a results file cannot say whether it tested the wheel or the bundle. I also recorded where the finding overstates: P5-9's PATH value does coincide under the driver's `env -i`, so that property is exercised even though the launcher's builder is not.

Severity: I agree with Medium — `check_bundle.sh` still covers P5-3/P5-4/P5-6/P5-9 on the real bundle; only the clean-account half is untested. Product suite unchanged at 1368 passed, 2 skipped (the 92 failures in the full run are other verifiers' red reproduction files).

